# Deferred, links

- A paste into the chat composer keeps `[[…]]` as text. To link it, mount
  `WikilinkPasteExtension` there with a paste catalog (without one it converts nothing)
  and spell full URIs as chat links do.
- Unfiled and Uploads documents aren't candidates for a pasted `[[Name]]`
  (`pasteTargets` in `features/editor/EditorView.tsx`). Decide whether they should be
  linkable by name.
- `[[Name#Heading]]` pastes labeled `Name`; Obsidian shows `Name > Heading`
  (`scanWikilinks` in `wikilink-paste.ts`).
- A pasted link keeps Obsidian's heading suffix as written (`Kael.md#The Duel`).
  Unverified: whether following it scrolls to the heading named by that text rather
  than a slug (`features/links/`).
- Every catalog revision starts a new resolution generation whose first read of a
  server-only key (a gone `doc:` ref, an unsettled ahead ref) is pending, which draws
  filled for one round trip before the dashed answer returns. Read the previous
  generation's answer while revalidating (`link-resolution.ts`,
  `features/links/project-link-resolver.ts`).
- Pasting a link with the caret directly after an identical link merges the two into
  one mark (`[Act 1Act 1](...)`), because ProseMirror joins adjacent equal marks. It
  should insert a separate link (`link-clipboard.ts`).
